<title>SOUTH KOREA: Sunkyong Sec to sell Fidelity funds.</title>
<headline>Sunkyong Sec to sell Fidelity funds.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sunkyong Securities Co said on Tuesday it would be the only company to sell in South Korea Fidelity's funds for investment in the U.S. and Asian equity markets.</p>
<p>Sunkyong signed the contract with Fidelity Investment Management (Hong Kong) Ltd, a Sunkyong official said.</p>
<p>Sunkyong expects to begin selling the funds from the middle of May after receiving approval from the Seoul government, a company official said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
